  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\sum_{k=0}^{n} T(n,k) = \\binom{2n+1}{n}, \\quad\\text{where}\\quad T(n,k) = \\binom{n+k}{k} - \\binom{n+k}{n+1}.",
    "plain": "Catalan's triangle is a two-parameter array of ballot numbers T(n,k), each counting monotone lattice paths from (0,0) to (n,k) that never rise above the main diagonal; its diagonal entries T(n,n) are the Catalan numbers. This problem asks us to sum an entire row: prove that T(n,0) + T(n,1) + ... + T(n,n) collapses to the single central-binomial value C(2n+1, n), aggregating the reflection-principle counts across the row and tying the triangle back to the Catalan/central-binomial family. The task is to formalize this row-sum identity in Lean 4 on top of the parent's already-verified ballotNumber object and its closed form.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Row sums close the loop between the Catalan triangle and the central-binomial sequence that generates it, showing that aggregating reflection-principle counts across a row reproduces C(2n+1, n).",
      "It is the natural next structural fact after the parent established individual entries, their closed form, and the lattice-path recurrence.",
      "Formalizing it exercises finite-sum manipulation of binomial coefficients (telescoping / hockey-stick aggregation), a recurring enumerative pattern with no dedicated Catalan-triangle instance in Mathlib."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
